% Test cases for the vacuum erection device policy (vacuum_erection.le):
% synthetic claims for L7900 and L7902, each fully documented, and each
% concluding nothing — the codes are statutorily non-covered (Policy Article
% A52712), so the claim fails at applicability whatever the record shows,
% and no change to the scenario makes it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base vacuum erection cases includes these resources:
    vacuum_erection.

the knowledge base vacuum erection cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a vacuum erection device (L7900): the standard
% written order, the delivery and its proof, a home — and no benefit.
scenario device_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the vacuum erection device.
    the HCPCS code of the vacuum erection device is "L7900".
    the vacuum erection device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the order for the vacuum erection device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the vacuum erection device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the vacuum erection device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the vacuum erection device includes order date.
    the order for the vacuum erection device includes description of the item.
    the order for the vacuum erection device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the vacuum erection device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the vacuum erection device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the vacuum erection device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the vacuum erection device.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
    flip expects changes [].

% The related accessories (L7902): the same.
scenario accessory is:
    claim 1 is for the tension rings.
    the HCPCS code of the tension rings is "L7902".
    the tension rings is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A claim dated before 1 July 2015: the current LCD text states no criteria
% for that period, so the model concludes nothing about it either.
scenario before_july_2015 is:
    claim 1 is for the vacuum erection device.
    the HCPCS code of the vacuum erection device is "L7900".
    the vacuum erection device is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2015-06-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A clinical justification in the record (erectile dysfunction following a
% radical prostatectomy, with the diagnosis code) changes nothing: the
% exclusion is statutory, not a matter of medical necessity — and no rule
% of the policy reads the diagnosis, so the record states only the claim.
scenario clinical_justification is:
    claim 1 is for the vacuum erection device.
    the HCPCS code of the vacuum erection device is "L7900".
    the vacuum erection device is furnished to Dee.
    the residence of Dee is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A code the policy does not decide (a penile prosthesis, L7900 misbilled as
% an implant code) is outside the scope of the model: not in scope, not
% decided.
scenario out_of_scope is:
    claim 1 is for the implant.
    the HCPCS code of the implant is "C1813".
    the implant is furnished to Eve.
    the residence of Eve is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
